From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shouchen <TheOneovb@petlover.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-raphael: give the tree the IDs ABL
 looks for

Xiaomi's ABL picks the device tree out of the boot image by matching
qcom,msm-id and qcom,board-id against the board it is running on. There is
no fallback: a DTB without these tags is not a candidate, and what is left
is a bootloader with nothing to boot.

Upstream board files do not carry them because the boot paths upstream
supports (U-Boot, UEFI) hand the tree over directly, so raphael's file was
written without them. Booting through the stock ABL -- which is what this
port does, to reuse the boot.img packing and the flash script it already
has -- needs them back.

Values read off this phone, not guessed:

  /proc/device-tree/qcom,board-id = <0x28 0>      (40)
  /proc/device-tree/qcom,msm-id   = <0x153 ...>   (339 = SM8150)

msm-id's second cell is the SoC revision and is written as 0x20000
(SM8150 v2.0), the revision this device's own boot image was built
against. A mismatch there fails the match just as a missing tag does, so
it is part of the same decision, not a detail.

Signed-off-by: shouchen <TheOneovb@petlover.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@ -31,6 +31,13 @@
 	chassis-type = "handset";
 
 	/*
+	 * Xiaomi's ABL selects the DTB by these two tags; see the commit
+	 * message for where the values come from.
+	 */
+	qcom,msm-id = <339 0x20000>;	/* SM8150 v2.0 */
+	qcom,board-id = <40 0>;
+
+	/*
 	 * Memory map as programmed by the bootloader.  sm8150.dtsi leaves the
 	 * size at 0 ("we expect the bootloader to fill in the size") and relies
 	 * on the board file for the real layout, so this is not optional: with
-- 
